This has already been done on NAO, actually; the vanilla method of 
seeding is only granular to the second, so it's trivial to reproduce
such a thing.  The person patched their local code to display a special
message with the time used to generate the seed if a wand of wishing 
was generated on DL1, cycled through a ton of game-starts for times
in the future, and then just waited for that particular time to start 
their game on NAO.

They then (in the interest of it remaining proof-of-concept) died by
kicking that same wand of wishing, so it was reported in-channel.  :)

The bug has since been patched on both NAO and Sporkhack.com to use a
more sophisticated method of generating the seed; I believe it has
already been reported to the Dev Team, as well, though I can't remember
(it was awhile ago).

